---
// Story 1-6. The home page. Replaces the story 1-2 deploy-chain placeholder.
//
// ⚠️ THE CI TRIPWIRE IS GONE ON PURPOSE. The old placeholder carried a
// MLW-SPIKE-1 marker that the deploy workflow asserted. That assertion was
// removed in the SAME commit as this page, which is what the 1-2 comment warned
// had to happen. The per-commit proof is dist/build-id.txt, which lives outside
// page content and is unaffected.
//
// COPY DIRECTION IS MANNY'S, AND DECISION 3 IS LOCKED (MN-48, confirmed by
// Keegan 2026-07-31): the h1 carries the SERVICE and the brand tagline sits
// above it as styled text. "Move Better, Live Longer" is a good brand line that
// tells a search engine, and a stranger, nothing about what Keegan does. For a
// business that needs to be found, a service-bearing h1 wins and the tagline
// loses nothing by sitting just above.
//
// Sections are ANSWER-FIRST (MN-48 decision 1): every h2 is a question a real
// person asks, and the first 40-60 words answer it outright before any context.
// The retrieval unit is a section, not a page — a section that builds to its
// answer mostly does not get extracted at all.
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import BookCta from '../components/BookCta.astro';
import business from '../data/business.json' with { type: 'json' };

const LAST_CHANGED = new Date('2026-07-31T00:00:00+10:00');
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Movement-Focused Chiropractor, Northern Beaches | ${business.name}`}
  description="Movement-focused chiropractic in Wheeler Heights on Sydney's Northern Beaches. Get out of pain, find out why it happened, and build a body that keeps up. 30-minute appointments with Keegan Baldwin."
  updated={LAST_CHANGED}
>
  <p class="brandline">{business.name} · Live Better, Longer</p>

  <h1>Movement-focused chiropractic on the Northern Beaches</h1>

  <p class="lead">Get out of pain, find why it happened, and build a body that keeps up.</p>

  <BookCta slug="new-patient" label="Book an appointment" showDetail={true} />

  <h2>What is movement-focused chiropractic?</h2>
  <p>
    It is chiropractic that treats how you move, not just where it hurts. I settle the acute problem,
    find the movement pattern behind it, and give you a plan so it stops coming back. Appointments
    are 30 minutes rather than 10, which is what makes that possible.
  </p>
  <p>
    If your shoulder, hip or knee is part of the problem, we address it. I combine spinal and joint
    adjustments with hands-on muscle release and massage, and I base your rehab on what your
    assessment actually showed rather than a generic sheet. Most patients need fewer visits overall.{' '}
    <a href="/services/chiropractic-treatment/">More about chiropractic and movement</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Who is this for?</h2>
  <p>
    Anyone in pain or stiffness who wants to know why, and anyone with no pain at all who wants more
    out of their body. Those are the same problem seen at two stages. All ages, demographics and
    levels of health and fitness are welcome.
  </p>

  <h2>What does it cost?</h2>
  <p>
    An initial consultation is $120 for one hour. A follow-up is $95 for 30 minutes. A Movement Plan
    Analysis, which is the full mobility assessment and personalised routine, is $160 for one hour.
    Treatments are health fund rebatable if you have chiropractic cover as an extra, and you can
    claim at the time of payment or later with an invoice.{' '}
    <a href="/services/">Full services and pricing</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Where are you, and when are you open?</h2>
  <p>
    I practise from {business.address.venue} at {business.address.streetAddress},{' '}
    {business.address.addressLocality}, on Sydney’s Northern Beaches. Full opening hours, the address
    and my phone number are at the bottom of every page on this site.
  </p>

  <h2>Can I try something smaller first?</h2>
  <p>
    Yes. Weekly group classes at Just Train Gym in Cromer are $20 for an hour and are designed as a
    low-commitment way to sample the same methods. There is a mobility and flexibility class and a
    handstand class, both open to complete beginners.{' '}
    <a href="/services/group-classes/">More about group classes</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Where to next?</h2>
  <ul class="next-links">
    <li><a href="/contact/">Book an appointment</a></li>
    <li><a href="/services/chiropractic-treatment/">Chiropractic &amp; Movement</a> — the main service page</li>
    <li><a href="/about/">About Keegan</a> — background and approach</li>
    <li><a href="/services/">Services and pricing</a></li>
  </ul>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* The brand line Decision 3 moved off the h1. Styled as a mark, not as a
     heading — it must not be an <h6> above the <h1>, which is exactly the
     decorative-heading mistake G-7 exists to stop the rebuild reproducing. */
  .brandline {
    margin: 0 0 0.35rem;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ml-muted);
  }
  h1 {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .lead {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
  }
  .next-links {
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
  }
  .next-links li {
    margin: 0.35rem 0;
  }
</style>
